        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1ed82b4b-42ef-553a-834b-81b93c6dd868",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hong Kong, Diamond Hill, Lantau Island, Ngong Ping\n- Organizations: Chi Lin Nunnery, Po Lin Monastery\n- Products: Tian Tan Buddha, Ngong Ping 360\n- Concepts: Buddhist temples, Tang Dynasty architectural style, tourist attractions\n\nFacts:\n- Chi Lin Nunnery is a prominent Buddhist temple in Diamond Hill, Hong Kong, and it was built in the Tang Dynasty architectural style.\n- Po Lin Monastery is a prominent Buddhist temple on Lantau Island in Hong Kong.\n- Tian Tan Buddha is a large outdoor bronze statue of Buddha Shakyamuni at Ngong Ping on Lantau Island in Hong Kong.\n- Tian Tan Buddha was completed in 1993.\n- Po Lin Monastery and Tian Tan Buddha are major tourist attractions that draw many visitors on weekends and holidays.\n- Ngong Ping 360 is home to Po Lin Monastery and Tian Tan Buddha.",
